[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I produced the feature group **`featuresa6c730`, version 1** on the Hopsworks platform (project `mlpab4f0925`, FG id 3462), entirely through the `hops` CLI with all compute running platform-side.
[agent] **What landed (verified via `hops fg info`/`features`/`preview`/`stats`):**
[agent] - Record key: `row_id` (string, primary); event-time: `event_time` (bigint, epoch ms)
[agent] - Exact columns: `row_id, account_id, event_time, amount_usd, is_weekend, amount_7d`
[agent] - `online_enabled: true` — features are available for low-latency online lookup as well as offline (the platform distinguishes the two stores)
[agent] - 700 rows — one per input row
[agent] **How the work ran on the platform:**
[agent] 1. Created/ingested two source FGs — `transactions_raw` (v1) and `fx_rates` (v1) — from the CSVs via `hops fg create` + `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. Ran the transformation as a **PySpark job on the platform** (`hops job deploy … --type pyspark --run --wait`, status SUCCEEDED). The job read the source FGs and computed:
[agent]    - `amount_usd` = `amount × fx_rate` (currency join)
[agent]    - `is_weekend` = 1 for Sat/Sun in UTC, via timezone-independent epoch arithmetic `(floor(event_time/86400000) + 4) % 7 ∈ {0,6}`, cross-checked against the calendar
[agent]    - `amount_7d` = per-account `SUM(amount)` over a Spark `RANGE BETWEEN 7-days PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW` window (inclusive both ends), on raw amount
[agent] 3. Wrote the result to the online-enabled target FG with `parents=[transactions_raw, fx_rates]` for lineage.
[agent] **One interface note (not a blocker):** the `hops sql` (Trino) path could not read the feature-group offline tables — both the `iceberg` and `hudi` connectors rejected them with `UNSUPPORTED_TABLE_TYPE` (the Python-engine writes produced tables neither connector recognizes). The window aggregation therefore could not be expressed in Trino; I used the Spark-job path instead, which is the canonical feature-pipeline approach and worked cleanly. Trino also required `--no-verify` due to an IP-SAN certificate mismatch on the query node.
